PR updated: a declared priority is now never changed. Constraints reorder a listener only among the ones sharing its priority, and a constraint that would need to cross a priority fails the build, naming both priorities. A listener that declares none (`AsEventListener::$priority` is now nullable) is placed by its constraints and takes the priority its place needs. That also settles @stof's question above: nothing is rewritten, so the runtime sort can't disagree with the compile-time order.

